{
  "_doc": "Stream C (play-test 5: T9 crates, T20 gift boxes). A crate is an item that opens into ONE random item of a named kind with a minimum rarity (js/rules/crates.js). `min` maps the quest vocabulary (stream E: common | uncommon | rare | epic | legendary) and the loot words (normal | magic | rare | legendary | unique) to Farhold's roll: `floor` = the lowest rarity the roll may come out as (null = any), `boost` = the rarity roll's luck multiplier, `show` = the rarity the crate ITSELF is drawn as. `slots` names what a slot word may open into as loot-pool families (data/rules/loot-pool.json); `weapon`, `offhand` and the armour slots are narrowed to what the opener's class uses (`forClass`, on unless the crate says false). `offhandFor` = which off-hand families a class gets: by its shield flag, its primary attribute and whether it shoots a bow. `names` are the crate's own names by slot. `maxAbove` = a crate never rolls more than this many levels above the level it was given at (its `maxLevel`), so a level-2 quest crate kept for later cannot become a level-40 item.",
